            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked how long the arbitration stay was intended to last."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eb41cb581fc64cce0ecb96f4f806d61dfcc2d6e744a85a4e4480a75739752065",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eb41cb581fc6-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer remarked that the question was obvious and followed from earlier discussion."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eb41cb581fc64cce0ecb96f4f806d61dfcc2d6e744a85a4e4480a75739752065",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eb41cb581fc6-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer answered that the contract means the parties promised not to go to court."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eb41cb581fc64cce0ecb96f4f806d61dfcc2d6e744a85a4e4480a75739752065",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eb41cb581fc6-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether California substantive law was being incorporated."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eb41cb581fc64cce0ecb96f4f806d61dfcc2d6e744a85a4e4480a75739752065",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eb41cb581fc6-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 58,
              "start": 58
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg inquired about the role of the Labor Commissioner in the arbitration process."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eb41cb581fc64cce0ecb96f4f806d61dfcc2d6e744a85a4e4480a75739752065",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eb41cb581fc6-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Brunstad, mr. Brunstad explained that disputes under the California Talent Agencies Act must first be presented to the California Labor Commissioner, after which either party may appeal to the Superior Court and invoke arbitration rules."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eb41cb581fc64cce0ecb96f4f806d61dfcc2d6e744a85a4e4480a75739752065",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eb41cb581fc6-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Brunstad, mr. Brunstad stated that the Labor Commissioner does not have judicial authority to finally decide the controversy."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eb41cb581fc64cce0ecb96f4f806d61dfcc2d6e744a85a4e4480a75739752065",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eb41cb581fc6-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Brunstad, mr. Brunstad noted that if an arbitration clause were invalid or fraudulent, the court would decide its arbitrability, citing First Options."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Schleimer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eb41cb581fc64cce0ecb96f4f806d61dfcc2d6e744a85a4e4480a75739752065",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eb41cb581fc6-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 58,
              "start": 58
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Mr. Schleimer argued that Judge Ferrer could involve the Labor Commissioner to obtain evidence, emphasizing the Commissioner\u2019s executive\u2011branch function."
      }
    ],
